{"assignees":[],"author":{"id":"U_kgDOCdbRxQ","is_bot":false,"login":"ACertainArchangel","name":""},"body":"# $300 Bounty — Render a Coherent Image on an E-ink display from the Quartz64A\n\nI do not currently know the scope of the fix required, and it may require well over $300's worth of engineering power. Consider the payout a gesture of appreciation for an awesome OSS contribution. \n\nMaximilian Weigand has done work on a device tree containing the EBC for the Q64A with a goal to get [PineNote linux](https://git.sr.ht/~hrdl/linux/log/v6.19_quartz64) working on it, which suggests he has worked towards or even accomplished this task before but I was unable to replicate a working PineNote distro on Q64A myself. \n\nThis repository is an attempt at being able to display an arbitrary greyscale image on an SE1030NE49-MNG-A0 e-ink display (which seems electrically identical to the [ED103TC2](https://files.pine64.org/doc/quartz64/Eink%20P-511-828-V1_ED103TC2%20Formal%20Spec%20V1.0_20190514.pdf) used in the pine-note; they are both 10.3\" Carta 1000) using a Quartz64 model A.\n\nSo far, upon boot, we just get shifting vertical lines (a failed attempt at running the INIT waveform) and a panel that is totally unresponsive from userspace.\n\nAn acceptable solution that satisfies this bounty will satisfy the following requirements:\n* Is a github repo newly shared with me or a PR to this repo\n* Facilitates the display of any pre-uploaded or dynamically generated image in 16-shade greyscale from userspace\n* Uses linux\n* Uses a display with an identical datasheet to the SE1030NE49-MNG-A0 (examples of acceptable displays are ED103TC2 and TWE1030NE48-MNG-A0, contact if you're not sure your display counts; datasheet found [here](https://files.pine64.org/doc/quartz64/Eink%20P-511-828-V1_ED103TC2%20Formal%20Spec%20V1.0_20190514.pdf))\n* Works on or can be easily made to work on both our Quartz64As/display setups\n* Functions out of the box with similar building and flashing infrastructure as is found in this repo's \"[build-and-flash.sh](https://github.com/ACertainArchangel/pinenote-on-q64a/blob/main/build-and-flash.sh)\"\n* Must be demonstrated rendering on real hardware\n\nFor more information on technical details, specifications/requirements, or to talk to me about claiming the bounty, I made a discord server, which I may also use for future bounties:\n\nhttps://discord.gg/NnvDkmqjk\n\nAlso possibly useful is a conversation I had in the Pine64 discord (the linked message up to where I send a video): [link](https://discord.com/channels/463237927984693259/811213663150407691/1518712092423753728)\n\nCurrent state of my particular setup here (which you don't necessarily have to build off):\n*EBC controller probes cleanly; loads 4-bit PVI waveform 0x19; /dev/fb0 comes up at 1872×1404.\n*tps65185 PMIC is driven — rails (VGH/VGL/VPOS/VNEG/VCOM) measured present and in-spec on a multimeter. (Steady-state only; sequencing during refresh not yet scoped.)\n*INIT waveform appears to start (LUT prints, lines shift once [video in the pine64 discord]) but never runs the expected BLACK→WHITE→BLACK→WHITE flash.\n*All userspace attempts to drive the display so far are complete no-ops — no refresh, no timeout, nothing logged.\n*Vertical lines shift randomly on each reset. Per hrdl, this points away from a waveform issue (that'd be location-independent) and toward a DT/timing/config problem.\n*Running hrdl's rockchip_ebc 0.3.0 on v6.19_pinenote, with Maximilian's rk3566-quartz64-a.dts unpatched.\n\nhttps://www.task-bounty.com/task/pinenote-on-q64a-1-300-bounty-render-a-coherent-im-iqmi9u\n\nP.S. / Edit: To be clear, when [chico10117](https://github.com/chico10117) said \"Would you consider an owner-run hardware verification path for this bounty?\" I thought he had a PineNote, or a Q64A and some other panel, not nothing. For future reference, completely unverified PR's that have never touched hardware do not meet the specs. Pull requests coming from autonomous AI agents or pull requests that have not been tested on any kind of hardware will be closed. Real humans with real hardware using AI assistive tools are welcome as long as you verify your fixes.\n","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOTCG1qc8AAAABHvX-Cw","author":{"login":"chico10117"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Hi, I do not have a matching Quartz64A / SE1030NE49-MNG-A0-class e-ink setup locally, so I do not want to claim this as-is or submit something that cannot be proven on real hardware.\\n\\nWould you consider an owner-run hardware verification path for this bounty? For example: I prepare a focused Linux/device-tree/userspace patch branch with build/flash instructions and a deterministic 16-shade greyscale test image/command, then you run it on your hardware. If it renders correctly on the real panel and meets the issue criteria, the bounty can be accepted through TaskBounty.\\n\\nIf that path is acceptable, the useful starting details would be: exact kernel branch/commit you want used, current DTS or overlay state, waveform file/source, panel variant, current serial/dmesg output around the userspace no-op refresh attempt, and whether TaskBounty payout can settle as USDC on Base. If hardware-local verification by the solver is mandatory, no problem; I will leave this for someone with the device.","createdAt":"2026-06-27T00:46:39Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/ACertainArchangel/pinenote-on-q64a/issues/1#issuecomment-4814405131","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOTCG1qc8AAAABH3nh-A","author":{"login":"pgwipeout"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Do you have a datasheet for the panel you are using?","createdAt":"2026-06-27T23:49:04Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/ACertainArchangel/pinenote-on-q64a/issues/1#issuecomment-4823048696","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOTCG1qc8AAAABIERqcg","author":{"login":"ACertainArchangel"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Hello. Yes, to answer these questions:\n\n1. I would be happy to do the verification for your software, [chico10117](https://github.com/chico10117). What kind of hardware do you have?\n\n2. And here is the datasheet, pgwipeout.\n\n[10.3.pdf](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/29479030/10.3.pdf)","createdAt":"2026-06-29T19:37:47Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/ACertainArchangel/pinenote-on-q64a/issues/1#issuecomment-4836321906","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOTCG1qc8AAAABIF00Xw","author":{"login":"chico10117"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Thanks. I do not have matching Quartz64A / 10.3-inch e-ink hardware locally; the viable path from my side is still owner-run verification on your setup.\n\nIf that is acceptable for this bounty, I can prepare a focused branch/PR against your repo with:\n\n- exact build/flash instructions matching `build-and-flash.sh`\n- a deterministic 16-shade greyscale test image/userspace command\n- logging points around EBC probe, waveform load, fb0 setup, and refresh trigger\n- small DTS/driver changes only, so you can bisect/run them on the real panel\n\nBefore I start implementation, can you confirm two things?\n\n1. A solution developed without local hardware, but demonstrated by you on your Quartz64A/display setup, can satisfy the `Must be demonstrated rendering on real hardware` requirement.\n2. TaskBounty payout can be settled to Base USDC, or another crypto rail that can be sent to a standard wallet.\n\nThe most useful technical inputs would be the exact kernel branch/commit you want targeted, your current DTS or overlay diff if it differs from this repo, the waveform file/source you are loading, and a fresh serial/dmesg log from boot through one userspace refresh attempt that currently no-ops.","createdAt":"2026-06-29T22:48:44Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/ACertainArchangel/pinenote-on-q64a/issues/1#issuecomment-4837946463","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOTCG1qc8AAAABIF17Vw","author":{"login":"chico10117"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Quick correction from my side: because I do not have matching Quartz64A / 10.3-inch e-ink hardware locally, I should not take this bounty forward or ask you to spend time testing speculative patches from me.\n\nPlease disregard my previous implementation-readiness request unless I later have compatible hardware available. I will leave this for someone who can develop and test on the real display before claiming/submitting.","createdAt":"2026-06-29T22:50:12Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/ACertainArchangel/pinenote-on-q64a/issues/1#issuecomment-4837964631","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOTCG1qc8AAAABIGTpNA","author":{"login":"ACertainArchangel"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"No worries. I just thought you meant you had a different display. It's not a problem. Thanks, Claude. 😉","createdAt":"2026-06-29T23:30:39Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[{"content":"HEART","users":{"totalCount":1}}],"url":"https://github.com/ACertainArchangel/pinenote-on-q64a/issues/1#issuecomment-4838451508","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOTCG1qc8AAAABIxgzEw","author":{"login":"ACertainArchangel"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"To be clear, when [chico10117](https://github.com/chico10117) said \"Would you consider an owner-run hardware verification path for this bounty?\" I thought he had a PineNote, or a Q64A and some other panel, not nothing. For future reference, completely unverified PR's that have never touched hardware do not meet the specs. Pull requests coming from autonomous AI agents or pull requests that have not been tested on *any* kind of hardware will be closed. Real humans with real hardware using AI assistive tools are welcome as long as you verify your fixes. Thanks!\n\nP.S. I'll also put this in the body of the issue so it's highly visible.","createdAt":"2026-07-04T20:45:24Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/ACertainArchangel/pinenote-on-q64a/issues/1#issuecomment-4883755795","viewerDidAuthor":false}],"createdAt":"2026-06-26T19:31:58Z","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDOTCG1qc8AAAACofOySQ","name":"help wanted","description":"Extra attention is needed","color":"008672"}],"state":"OPEN","title":"$300 Bounty — Render a Coherent Image on an E-ink display from the Quartz64A","updatedAt":"2026-07-04T20:46:00Z","url":"https://github.com/ACertainArchangel/pinenote-on-q64a/issues/1"}
